    {
      "type": "SetFeature",
      "args": {
        "featureName": "vector_lights",
        "enabled": "true"
      },
      "description": "THE SHIPPED DEFAULT, and the one arm here that lets the clock run. With leaf tracking on, the glow-grid hole is not opened by the notification -- it is opened by GameComponent_DoorAperture when the leaves finish sliding. Nothing above can test that, because a paused scenario never advances OpenPct. This arm opens the door with the clock running, waits out the swing, and then asks vanilla's own gameplay light whether the doorway became a hole."
    },
    {
      "type": "SetFeature",
      "args": {
        "featureName": "vector_light_penumbra",
        "enabled": "true"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "SetFeature",
      "args": {
        "featureName": "vector_light_suppress",
        "enabled": "true"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "SetFeature",
      "args": {
        "featureName": "vector_light_blend",
        "enabled": "true"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "SetFeature",
      "args": {
        "featureName": "vector_light_mask",
        "enabled": "true"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "SetFeature",
      "args": {
        "featureName": "vector_light_mask_beam",
        "enabled": "true"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "SetFeature",
      "args": {
        "featureName": "vector_light_open_doors",
        "enabled": "true"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "SetFeature",
      "args": {
        "featureName": "vector_light_door_glow_blocker",
        "enabled": "true"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "SetFeature",
      "args": {
        "featureName": "vector_light_door_aperture",
        "enabled": "true"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "SetDoorOpen",
      "args": {
        "offset": "0,45",
        "open": "false"
      },
      "description": "Shut first, so the swing this arm measures is a real one from zero."
    },
    {
      "type": "SetTimeSpeed",
      "args": {
        "speed": "normal"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "SetDoorOpen",
      "args": {
        "offset": "0,45",
        "open": "true"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "Wait",
      "args": {
        "frames": "60"
      },
      "description": "Long enough for the leaves to finish: a wooden door slides in well under 60 ticks, and the same 60 is what vector_light_door_close uses to settle a swing."
    },
    {
      "type": "SetTimeSpeed",
      "args": {
        "speed": "paused"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "Probe",
      "args": {
        "probeName": "door_aperture",
        "expectedValue": "1",
        "tolerance": "0.001"
      },
      "description": "THE SWING ACTUALLY FINISHED, pinned next to the effect so a change to the clock, the door's material or the Wait length fails loudly here instead of silently emptying the assertion below. This is the QUANTISED aperture -- the same expression the glow-grid rule reads, which is the whole of the fix: reading the raw ratio here instead ended the swing at 0.956 and refused the hole one call before anything asked again."
    },
    {
      "type": "Probe",
      "args": {
        "probeName": "door_aperture_watched",
        "expectedValue": "0",
        "tolerance": "0.001"
      },
      "description": "And the door left the watch set, which is what makes the assertion below a ONE-SHOT question: nothing sweeps this door again, so a rule that answered 'not yet' at the end of the slide never gets a second chance."
    },
    {
      "type": "Probe",
      "args": {
        "probeName": "vector_light_lit_area",
        "expectedValue": "468.896484",
        "tolerance": "2"
      },
      "description": "OUR OWN POLYGON, pinned at the drawn-only arm's value to the last decimal. This is the probe answer to whether the silhouette memo needs invalidating when the bit moves: the animated path and the instant path must build the SAME polygon, and a memo still holding 'this cell is a wall' across the swing would show here as the shut door's 455.4963. It does not, because ReconcileGlowBlocker's LightBlockerRemoved comes back through Patch_VectorLightBlockerRemoved with blockerMoved true and drops the record."
    },
    {
      "type": "Probe",
      "args": {
        "probeName": "vector_light_shadow_fraction",
        "expectedValue": "0.280377477",
        "tolerance": "0.01"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "Probe",
      "args": {
        "probeName": "vector_light_verts",
        "expectedValue": "452",
        "tolerance": "6"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "Probe",
      "args": {
        "probeName": "door_outside_ground_glow",
        "expectedValue": "0.5",
        "tolerance": "0.005"
      },
      "description": "THE ASSERTION. Vanilla's own GroundGlowAt beyond a FULLY SLID door. 0.0951 is what a blocked doorway delivers here and 0.5 is what a hole in the wall does, so this separates 'the bit moved' from 'the bit never moved' by a factor of five rather than by a tolerance."
    },
    {
      "type": "Probe",
      "args": {
        "probeName": "door_inside_ground_glow",
        "expectedValue": "0.5",
        "tolerance": "0.005"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "Screenshot",
      "args": {
        "fileName": "opendoor_tracked_open_glowgrid.png"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "SetTimeSpeed",
      "args": {
        "speed": "normal"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "SetDoorOpen",
      "args": {
        "offset": "0,45",
        "open": "false"
      },
      "description": "AND BACK. The bit is restored on the FIRST tick of a close rather than at the end of one, so this also pins that a door told to shut stops being a hole immediately -- the asymmetry DoorApertureMath.GlowGridHoleWanted describes."
    },
    {
      "type": "Wait",
      "args": {
        "frames": "60"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "SetTimeSpeed",
      "args": {
        "speed": "paused"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "Probe",
      "args": {
        "probeName": "door_outside_ground_glow",
        "expectedValue": "0.0951154977",
        "tolerance": "0.005"
      },
      "description": "Back to exactly what a shut door delivers: turning the door back into a blocker has to restore vanilla, not leave the hole standing."
    },
    {
      "type": "Probe",
      "args": {
        "probeName": "door_aperture_watched",
        "expectedValue": "0",
        "tolerance": "0.001"
      },
      "description": "The close is over too. A door left in the set would keep dirtying geometry every tick for the rest of the session, which no frame shows and no other probe here would catch."
    },
    {
      "type": "Screenshot",
      "args": {
        "fileName": "opendoor_tracked_shut_glowgrid.png"
      }
    }
  ]
}
